Add `extensions.pr-watch`, `extensions.remote-run` and `extensions.teleport`
to Kimchi's resource registry and route the three extensions through
`enabledExtensionFactories`. `isRemoteRunEnabled()` also honours the
remote-run resource, so every caller gated on it (ferment and permissions
"run in cloud" choices) goes quiet when the resource is off.

Remote run and teleport default to true. PR watch defaults to false: its
model-callable `pr_watch` tool starts with `autoFix` true, so one call lets
the model edit, commit and push to a PR, and a confirmed offer re-arms in
later sessions. `isPRMonitoringPermitted()` honours the resource too, which
keeps the extension inert under ACP, and the ACP server neither advertises
`prMonitoring` nor intercepts `/pr-watch` prompts or lists the command while
it is off.

